<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-16">16 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Ford Motor Company is incorporated</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ford">Henry Ford</a> and eleven investors founded the company in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/detroit">Detroit</a>. Its Model T and moving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assembly-line">assembly line</a> made cars affordable to millions.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-17">17 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Wright brothers make the first powered flights</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At Kill Devil Hills near Kitty Hawk, North Carolina, Orville Wright flew the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wright-flyer">Wright Flyer</a> for 12 seconds and about 37 metres. Of four flights that day, Wilbur's longest lasted 59 seconds.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/hay-bunau-varilla-treaty" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hay-bunau-varilla-treaty.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/hay-bunau-varilla-treaty">Hay–Bunau-Varilla Treaty</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Hay–Bunau-Varilla Treaty was signed on 18 November 1903 by US Secretary of State John Hay and Philippe Bunau-Varilla, acting for the newly independent Panama.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/hay-herran-treaty" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hay-herran-treaty.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/hay-herran-treaty">Hay–Herrán Treaty</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Hay–Herrán Treaty was signed in January 1903 by US Secretary of State John Hay and the Colombian chargé d'affaires Tomás Herrán.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/may-coup-serbia" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/may-coup-serbia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolution</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/may-coup-serbia">May Coup (Serbia)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The May Coup was the assassination of King Alexander Obrenović of Serbia and his wife Draga by army officers in Belgrade in June 1903 (May by the Julian calendar).</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-petropolis">Treaty of Petrópolis</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty of Petrópolis, signed on 17 November 1903, ended the dispute between Bolivia and Brazil over Acre, a rubber-rich Amazon territory settled by Brazilian rubber tappers who had rebelled against Bolivian rule.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolt</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/ilinden-preobrazhenie-uprising">Ilinden–Preobrazhenie Uprising</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Ilinden–Preobrazhenie Uprising was a revolt against Ottoman rule organised by the Internal Macedonian-Adrianople Revolutionary Organisation in August 1903.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-burmi">Battle of Burmi</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Burmi was fought in 1903 in north-eastern Nigeria between British colonial forces and followers of the deposed caliph Attahiru I, who had fled after the fall of Sokoto.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-kiganda">Treaty of Kiganda</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty of Kiganda was the agreement of June 1903 by which Mwami Mwezi IV Gisabo of Burundi submitted to German authority after years of resistance and a German punitive campaign.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/british-conquest-of-kano">British conquest of Kano</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The British conquest of Kano took place in February 1903, when forces of the Protectorate of Northern Nigeria under Frederick Lugard captured the city after a brief engagement.</p></div></li></ol></section>
