<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/sokoto-caliphate"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Sokoto%20Caliphate.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Sokoto Caliphate</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">British forces take Kano in February and occupy Sokoto in March</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/sokoto-caliphate"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Sokoto%20Caliphate.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Sokoto Caliphate</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Sultan Attahiru I is killed fighting the British at Burmi in July</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-bolivia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Bolivia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Bolivia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Treaty of Petrópolis cedes Acre to Brazil</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-panama"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Panama.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Panama</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Panama declares independence from Colombia and signs the Hay–Bunau-Varilla Treaty</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/aceh-sultanate"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Aceh%20Sultanate.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Aceh Sultanate</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Sultan Muhammad Daud Syah surrenders to the Dutch</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-colombia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Colombia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Colombia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Panama secedes with United States support</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-burundi"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Burundi.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Burundi</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Mwezi IV submits to German rule in the Treaty of Kiganda</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/womens-suffrage-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Women's%20suffrage%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Women's suffrage movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Emmeline Pankhurst founds the Women’s Social and Political Union in Manchester</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/kalinago"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kalinago.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kalinago</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The British government grants the Kalinago a territory of 3,700 acres on the east coast of Dominica</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/anarchism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Anarchism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Anarchism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The United States passes the Immigration Act of 1903, also called the Anarchist Exclusion Act</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-serbia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Serbia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Serbia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">In the May Coup officers kill King Alexander I and Queen Draga; Peter Karađorđević becomes Peter I</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/khartoum"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Khartoum.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Khartoum</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Gordon Memorial College opens</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/albert-einstein"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Albert%20Einstein.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Albert Einstein</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Marries Mileva Marić in January; the Swiss Patent Office makes his position as assistant examiner permanent</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/vladimir-lenin"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Vladimir%20Lenin.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Vladimir Lenin</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">At the second Congress of the Russian Social Democratic Labour Party in London the party splits into Lenin's Bolsheviks and Martov's Mensheviks</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/marie-curie"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Marie%20Curie.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Marie Curie</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Awarded her doctorate and, in December, shares the Nobel Prize in Physics with Pierre Curie and Henri Becquerel</span></li></ul></section>
